WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.200 --> 00:00:02.367
-Wow.
It looks good on you, bud.

00:00:02.367 --> 00:00:03.200
-Thank you.

00:00:03.200 --> 00:00:04.868
-Are you used to wearing it?

00:00:04.868 --> 00:00:06.267
-Yeah, now, after today, yeah.

00:00:06.267 --> 00:00:07.667
[ Laughter ]
-Yeah.

00:00:07.667 --> 00:00:12.434
You're going to college at Yale,
so you're a college student.

00:00:12.434 --> 00:00:13.534
-Right.
-Really, yeah.

00:00:13.534 --> 00:00:15.634
And now you got to go back
to college.

00:00:15.634 --> 00:00:18.267
[ Laughter ]
-Yeah. Yep.

00:00:18.267 --> 00:00:22.067
-Yeah, but you just won
the gold medal in the Olympics.

00:00:22.067 --> 00:00:23.734
How are you going to do this?
You can't wear this

00:00:23.734 --> 00:00:25.801
around campus.
-No, no, absolutely not.

00:00:25.801 --> 00:00:26.868
It's going to be great.
I mean,

00:00:26.868 --> 00:00:28.367
I'm pretty excited for that,
back to

00:00:28.367 --> 00:00:30.033
-Going back to
-[Both] normal life.

00:00:30.033 --> 00:00:32.501
-What else are you excited
about, taking naps?

00:00:32.501 --> 00:00:33.567
[ Laughter ]
-Oh, absolutely.

00:00:33.567 --> 00:00:34.801
I mean, I just got back
from Beijing

00:00:34.801 --> 00:00:36.234
like last night, so.
-Do you have any idea

00:00:36.234 --> 00:00:37.901
where you are?
-No, I have no idea.

00:00:37.901 --> 00:00:39.767
[ Laughter ]
-Yeah.

00:00:39.767 --> 00:00:41.434
I was rooting for you,
obviously,

00:00:41.434 --> 00:00:43.467
going into the Olympics and I
was like, "Oh, my gosh."

00:00:43.467 --> 00:00:46.467
I go, "I want this kid
to nail it."

00:00:46.467 --> 00:00:49.567
And you go out there
and I've never seen anything

00:00:49.567 --> 00:00:50.667
more beautiful in my life.

00:00:50.667 --> 00:00:52.868
You were unbelievable.
-Thank you.

00:00:52.868 --> 00:00:56.467
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:00:56.467 --> 00:00:59.200
-It was almost like watching
a magic trick or something.

00:00:59.200 --> 00:01:01.868
Because I've never seen --
You jump up.

00:01:01.868 --> 00:01:03.501
They call you the Quad King.
-[ Laughs ]

00:01:03.501 --> 00:01:08.267
-Because you do four spins
and then land.

00:01:08.267 --> 00:01:09.868
Does it matter what skate
you land on?

00:01:09.868 --> 00:01:11.734
-Generally, yeah.
So, if you are right-handed,

00:01:11.734 --> 00:01:13.400
you generally always land
on your right.

00:01:13.400 --> 00:01:14.968
But there are some exceptions
to that.

00:01:14.968 --> 00:01:17.434
There are some athletes that are
like able to do it both ways,

00:01:17.434 --> 00:01:18.467
but I just land on my right.

00:01:18.467 --> 00:01:19.767
-How do you know
that you can do that?

00:01:19.767 --> 00:01:21.300
I mean, obviously,
you practice and try,

00:01:21.300 --> 00:01:22.567
[ Laughter ]
but I mean --
-Right, right.

00:01:22.567 --> 00:01:24.334
-Do you know,
once you spring up,

00:01:24.334 --> 00:01:26.334
that it's going to work
or not work?

00:01:26.334 --> 00:01:28.567
-Generally yeah, yeah.
I would say like,

00:01:28.567 --> 00:01:31.167
more often than not,
athletes will go into the jump

00:01:31.167 --> 00:01:33.100
and then if it happens
to go the way that we want,

00:01:33.100 --> 00:01:34.300
you'll see it work.

00:01:34.300 --> 00:01:35.934
Right off the takeoff,
if something goes awful,

00:01:35.934 --> 00:01:37.834
bail out and so,
instead of doing four revs,

00:01:37.834 --> 00:01:40.200
we'll do like maybe two
or three revolutions.

00:01:40.200 --> 00:01:42.601
But, yeah, that'll be a big
error, if we were to do that.

00:01:42.601 --> 00:01:44.200
-And now, when that happens,

00:01:44.200 --> 00:01:46.167
are you just bummed
for the rest of the routine?

00:01:46.167 --> 00:01:47.467
[ Laughter ]
Because you go,

00:01:47.467 --> 00:01:49.267
"I'm not going to win the gold
at this point."

00:01:49.267 --> 00:01:51.067
And then you're like trying
to smile and go,

00:01:51.067 --> 00:01:53.200
"Yeah, this is my thing,
but, yeah, I messed up."

00:01:53.200 --> 00:01:56.634
-To an extent, I would say yes.
You have to like put on a smile

00:01:56.634 --> 00:01:57.834
and be like, "Whatever,
I have to finish it."

00:01:57.834 --> 00:01:59.434
-Yeah.
Are you hard on yourself?

00:01:59.434 --> 00:02:00.901
-Yeah, I'd say so.
I mean,

00:02:00.901 --> 00:02:02.734
we're all pretty competitive,
so we want to do well.

00:02:02.734 --> 00:02:04.968
-Yeah. Did you get to see
what you did

00:02:04.968 --> 00:02:06.100
or do you not watch
what you did?

00:02:06.100 --> 00:02:08.067
-I have, yeah, I did.
I got to watch it.

00:02:08.067 --> 00:02:09.934
-It was unbelievable.
-Thank you.

00:02:10.000 --> 00:02:11.267
-It was unbelievable.
-Thank you.

00:02:11.267 --> 00:02:12.734
Nathan Chen.
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:02:12.734 --> 00:02:14.100
It was insane.

00:02:14.100 --> 00:02:16.767
Perfection.
It was like well done.

00:02:16.767 --> 00:02:19.167
How many jumps are there
in skating?

00:02:19.167 --> 00:02:20.400
-There are six jumps.
There are

00:02:20.400 --> 00:02:23.100
Axel, salchow, toe loop,
loop, flip, and Lutz.

00:02:23.100 --> 00:02:26.100
But minor details
between the six.

00:02:26.100 --> 00:02:29.100
-And can you do any of the jumps
when you're not wearing skates?

00:02:29.100 --> 00:02:30.501
[ Laughter ]

00:02:30.501 --> 00:02:32.400
-I mean, like to an extent, yes.
-I mean --

00:02:32.400 --> 00:02:35.534
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:02:35.534 --> 00:02:37.434
This might be the first time

00:02:37.434 --> 00:02:39.234
we've had a gold medalist
on the show.

00:02:39.234 --> 00:02:40.634
I mean, would you be able
-Sure.

00:02:40.634 --> 00:02:42.367
-to do a jump on our show?
-Sure, yeah.

00:02:42.367 --> 00:02:43.667
You could probably do an Axel.

00:02:43.667 --> 00:02:45.567
[ Cheering and applause ]
I'll put this down really quick.

00:02:45.567 --> 00:02:46.801
-Sure.
-Give this to you.

00:02:46.801 --> 00:02:47.901
-Oh, I'll take it.
Don't worry about it.

00:02:47.901 --> 00:02:49.267
Yeah, I got this.
Don't worry about that.

00:02:49.267 --> 00:02:51.634
-So, yeah,
you could do like a single Axel,

00:02:51.634 --> 00:02:54.267
where you step in, jump,
rotate, and land.

00:02:54.267 --> 00:02:57.200
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:02:57.200 --> 00:03:00.801
[ Rimshot ]
So, basically, that's that.

00:03:00.801 --> 00:03:02.467
But we do that like times three.

00:03:02.467 --> 00:03:04.200
So we do the same thing,
but rotate three times

00:03:04.200 --> 00:03:05.067
and then do that on the ice.

00:03:05.067 --> 00:03:06.334
-I could try one,

00:03:06.334 --> 00:03:07.901
but you'd have to show me.
-Please, please, please.

00:03:07.901 --> 00:03:09.067
[ Cheering and applause ]
I would love to.

00:03:09.067 --> 00:03:11.234
I'd love to.
-Slow motion, what do you do?

00:03:11.234 --> 00:03:12.801
-Alright.
So this is called an Axel.

00:03:12.801 --> 00:03:14.701
This is the one jump that we
take off going forward.

00:03:14.701 --> 00:03:16.133
Everything else goes backwards.

00:03:16.133 --> 00:03:17.334
-Axel goes forward.

00:03:17.334 --> 00:03:19.100
-You start off on the right.
-Yeah.

00:03:19.100 --> 00:03:20.701
-Step forward on the left.

00:03:20.701 --> 00:03:21.868
Kick through.

00:03:21.868 --> 00:03:24.367
And you rotate and then land
on your right.

00:03:24.367 --> 00:03:26.033
-So it's kind of like
the Electric Slide.

00:03:26.033 --> 00:03:27.567
Yeah, I understand.
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:03:27.567 --> 00:03:28.968
Alright.
-So let's like break it down.

00:03:28.968 --> 00:03:31.334
-When do you go up?
-Instead of doing a full rev,

00:03:31.334 --> 00:03:32.367
we'll just do half a rev.

00:03:32.367 --> 00:03:34.100
-Thank you.
-So you go here, jump up,

00:03:34.100 --> 00:03:35.200
jump, and land.

00:03:35.200 --> 00:03:36.067
[ Cheering and applause ]
There it is.

00:03:36.067 --> 00:03:36.834
There, there it is.

00:03:36.834 --> 00:03:39.167
[ Rimshot ]

00:03:39.167 --> 00:03:41.167
-Here, you deserve this more
than I do.

00:03:41.167 --> 00:03:43.367
This is the one and only
Nathan Chen right there.

00:03:43.367 --> 00:03:45.634
[ Cheering and applause ]
Olympic gold medalist.

